## Decision honesty

**FIXED path-A for CRIT 7.1 (`c_guard_scan_idents`):**

Walker is defined in `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo` (200 lines). Ident
spans are **one** `str_slice(args, start, i)` per token, then
`c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`. There is no `name = name + c` / per-char
OoStr concat in the walker. `.oo` has no C `char buf[N]`; the alpha honesty
for the SPRINT “stack buffer” wording is **slice-once-per-span** (same close
as `t1_memory.oot` M-SG1/M-SG2).

Live prove: `scripts/s71_guard_scan_smoke.sh` **ALL OK** (fail-closed IDENT
println + write_file payload; string-literal no-FP). T1/T2 secret smokes
that exercise the same walker remain exit 0.

**Still not claimed (do not greenwash):**

| Residual | Status |
|----------|--------|
| **7.10** `c_parse_secret_env` `name = name + c` | open — other OWN |
| **7.2** `c_sys_exec_last_arg` slice (sibling CRIT) | claimed sliced in source; **not** this close |
| `secret_sink_enforce` / `secret_product_floor` exit 1 | **doc path** `SECRET_TAINT.md` vs live `SECRET_TAINT.oot` — **not** emit/scan fail |
| `char_at` 1-byte `OoStr` temps while walking | language floor — not quadratic ident leak |
| Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interp `${}` | residual (named in harness + ideas) |
| C-text re-lex vs token-stream dual-path | residual (I2/I3 later; not this CRIT) |
| Interproc SECRET beyond same-file `__fr_secret__` | residual |
| Formal peer `.oot` still mid-land | ok — smoke + domain + integration hold close |

Path-A 7.1 ≠ C stack buffer rewrite.  
Cap preferred style: smoke green + named residual = FIXED path-A.  
**ALREADY_FIXED** path-A: source already sliced; this close is prove + board flip.

